We also offer a vast variety of instrumentals, sound engineering (mixing & mastering), album cover art and more! Donna  Summer   --    Hot   Stuff ::  Lyrics  :: Hot Stuff" is a song by American singer Donna Summer from her seventh studio album Bad Girls (1979), released as the lead single from Bad Girls on April 13, 1979, through Casablanca Records. Up to that point, Summer had mainly been associated with disco songs but this song also showed a significant rock direction, including a guitar solo by ex-Doobie Brother and Steely Dan guitarist Jeff "Skunk" Baxter. It is one of her most popular songs, based on the performance on the Billboard Hot 100...
